// Settings of the simulation itself (WP4.2, WP4.3, WP4.4), as opposed to the definitions of
// its units. Read by sf_data::sim_settings; sf_bridge hands them to the world.
// The rules they belong to are in docs/rules/pathfinding.md and docs/rules/collision.md.
//
// path_node_budget: how many nodes of path search work the simulation may do in
// one tick, for all units together. Every search step that expands a cell or a
// portal counts one. A bigger budget gives units their routes sooner (a crowd
// that is ordered at once is served in fewer ticks); it never changes which
// route a unit gets. It costs time in every tick the service has work, so it is
// the knob that trades the load of a big order against the frame time.
// At least 512 (a line of sight, the one step that cannot be cut, needs up to 60).
// Tests and scenarios that do not give a budget use the simulation's own
// default, which is the same number.
//
// flowfield_threshold: how many units of one movement class a single order must send to
// one place for the simulation to build one flowfield for them (WP4.3) instead of
// routing each on its own. A smaller number makes more orders groups: a field costs
// about as much as a handful of single routes and then serves any number of units,
// but it is built for one goal and a region, so a pair of units sent to different
// places is better off with a route each. 0 turns flowfields off (every unit is routed
// on its own); 1 is not a group and is refused; at most 1000.
// Tests and scenarios that do not give one use the simulation's own default, which is
// the same number.
//
// collision (WP4.4): whether units have bodies. A body is a disc of half the unit's `size`
// (unit_defs.ron); bodies are pushed apart, units that meet head-on keep right, a unit
// holding position is never pushed. false lets units pass through each other, as before WP4.4.
//
// wait_ticks: a unit that has not come closer to where it is going for this many ticks
// detours round what is in its way (a unit holding position, a unit coming the other way).
// 20 ticks are a second. At least 1.
//
// stuck_ticks: a unit that has not come closer for this many ticks steps to a free
// neighbouring spot. More than wait_ticks, at most 1000.
//
// stuck_attempts: after this many such steps in a row it asks for a new route (WP4.7): a
// new search from where it stands that goes round the bodies near it that stand still (a
// unit holding position). At least 1.
// Tests and scenarios that do not give them use the simulation's own defaults, which are
// the same numbers.
//
// replan_cooldown (WP4.7): ticks between two such requests of one unit; it sidesteps again
// meanwhile. 1 to 1000.
//
// replan_max (WP4.7): how many such requests one unit may make in one order. When it is
// stuck still after the last, the order is given up: its next queued order starts, or it
// stands idle where it is. 1 to 100.
//
// retarget_cooldown (WP4.7): ticks between two new searches of a unit that goes for a
// target that keeps moving (an attack, a guard of an entity). 1 to 1000.
(
    path_node_budget: 4096,
    flowfield_threshold: 8,
    collision: true,
    wait_ticks: 6,
    stuck_ticks: 60,
    stuck_attempts: 3,
    replan_cooldown: 100,
    replan_max: 3,
    retarget_cooldown: 20,
)
